-- erwartet: N054
-- **The other direction of the device tier: feature names were checked against nothing.**
--
-- Measured 2026-09-02, eleven written forms across six predicate positions: **64 of 66
-- accepted.** `Has()` with no argument, `Has(7)`, `Has(GRENZE + 1)`, `Has(T.slots)` and the
-- line below all gave `0 errors, 0 hints`. The two that fell did so at `N053` and about the
-- SECOND argument, not about the form.
--
-- **This one is the sharpest of the five, and it is why the rule is an error.**
-- `Has(RDTSCP, XSAVE)` reads as a demand for two features and is a demand for one: every
-- reader of the form takes `argumente.first()` -- `namen.rs::has_aus_pred` since
-- 2026-08-19 -- and the rest of the list has never been read by anybody. *A form whose
-- second half is silently dropped is the shape this folder pays for over and over.*
--
-- **What this rule deliberately does NOT decide: whether `RDTSCP` is a feature at all.**
-- `SPRACHE.md` puts the only generator of `Has(F)` at the CPUID probe (A14), that probe does
-- not exist, and nothing in the language declares a feature name. Checking the NAME needs a
-- declared list, and who declares it is an owner's decision -- a house table under `arch`,
-- the way `cnamen.rs::SIGNATUR` carries what C has taken, or a language form that mints the
-- witness. **The SHAPE needs neither, and that is what falls here.**

module gift::merkmalsforderung_fuer_zwei_merkmale {

axiom xsave_und_zeit() -> u64
    requires Has(RDTSCP, XSAVE)
    effects  { pure }
    unfalsifiable "two feature names under one demand, and the second is never read";

}
